{"title": "RealSense D456", "parts": {"lead": "<p class=lead>Depth camera from RealSense with a 95 mm global-shutter infrared stereo pair, a global-shutter RGB camera and a 6-axis IMU in an IP65 enclosure, built on the same D450 camera module as the D455. One hand-held recording in front of a chessboard on a screen, solved as left infrared + right infrared + RGB + IMU.</p><div class=chips><span class=chip>Global shutter</span><span class=chip>3 cameras</span><span class=chip>400 Hz IMU</span><span class=chip>IP65</span><span class=chip>CC BY-NC 4.0</span></div>", "glance": "<p>Depth camera from RealSense with a 95 mm global-shutter infrared stereo pair, a global-shutter RGB camera and a 6-axis IMU in an IP65 enclosure, built on the same D450 camera module as the D455. One hand-held recording in front of a chessboard on a screen, solved as left infrared + right infrared + RGB + IMU.</p><div class=band><figure class=demo><video src=\"/media/sensors/realsense-d456/demo.mp4\" poster=\"/media/sensors/realsense-d456/demo.jpg\" autoplay muted loop playsinline controls preload=metadata></video><figcaption>The 3D scene MVIS recovered from this recording.</figcaption></figure><div class=v data-v=\"0\"><div class=tiles><div><span>Reprojection median</span><b>0.06<small> px</small></b></div><div><span>cam0–cam1 baseline</span><b>94.4<small> mm</small></b></div><div><span>cam0 td</span><b>+7.08<small> ms</small></b></div><div><span>cam0 lever arm</span><b>35.5<small> mm</small></b></div></div></div></div><p class=sd-note>Reprojection is how far, in pixels, the detected corners lie from where the solve puts them. td is the camera–IMU time offset, and the lever arm is the camera–IMU position offset.</p><p class=sd-note>One recording, with no independent reference on this page. These values show what MVIS solved, not how close they are to the truth.</p>", "process": "<p>The path of the rig around the board, as MVIS solved it. To explore it:</p><ul class=list><li>Press <b>Play</b> or drag the bar to follow the path.</li><li>Use the <b>view buttons</b> to change the view.</li><li>Pick a <b>camera card</b> to put that camera on the frustum, the pyramid that shows its view.</li></ul><p>Each card draws the board from the solved pose, with the corners MVIS detected. We publish no camera images.</p><div class=v data-v=\"0\"><div class=proc-wrap><button type=button class=proc-open hidden><svg viewBox=\"0 0 400 220\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><polygon points=\"220.5,20.0 314.4,54.1 317.2,138.1 223.4,104.0 220.5,20.0\" fill=\"var(--strong)\" fill-opacity=\".1\" stroke=\"var(--muted)\"/><polyline points=\"166.8,135.9 166.9,135.8 166.5,136.0 164.4,136.9 162.1,137.8 159.5,138.7 156.8,139.7 156.3,140.3 160.0,140.5 159.7,140.2 160.9,139.5 161.7,140.6 158.3,141.3 147.1,143.2 140.2,145.9 135.4,149.1 125.5,152.4 122.3,152.6 123.8,152.8 131.2,150.1 140.4,146.0 152.0,142.0 173.1,131.4 177.2,126.1 181.6,123.2 138.2,136.9 139.0,136.5 140.5,137.4 141.9,136.6 148.2,133.6 157.6,125.3 180.5,121.9 165.0,127.1 154.9,132.9 151.8,136.7 140.4,140.6 131.6,145.9 124.6,149.4 131.4,147.5 148.0,142.3 164.3,138.1 177.8,132.2 189.5,127.9 184.2,129.7 164.1,134.7 142.6,143.2 130.3,149.2 115.6,156.3 107.0,161.5 115.7,157.3 133.8,148.2 152.8,140.3 166.6,136.7 163.8,137.7 147.7,144.9 121.9,155.4 107.4,161.5 105.8,164.9 127.0,157.3 146.6,149.7 157.3,145.5 141.7,152.4 107.9,165.0 82.8,182.2 104.2,170.3 130.1,157.0 150.0,150.8 145.7,153.7 124.6,160.9 118.1,169.4 128.3,155.7 123.7,162.4 125.3,167.9 126.6,173.4 131.2,172.4 135.9,169.9 132.2,171.4 132.2,169.4 131.5,169.4 130.7,169.9 132.1,167.4 125.8,166.6 130.8,171.7 136.0,174.8 138.3,176.3 136.1,170.4 133.2,172.8 127.6,173.3 137.9,167.7 135.1,170.4 136.1,170.0 135.1,169.3 142.7,164.1 142.0,165.5 140.5,167.0 138.6,167.0 148.0,163.8 146.4,164.8 145.7,165.4 143.4,164.4 145.1,161.0 148.0,161.4 148.2,164.6 147.8,165.8 147.3,161.5 146.1,161.6 147.9,169.2 141.2,164.7 136.4,164.6 150.9,173.4 140.3,167.8 153.8,177.1 145.4,167.8 163.5,156.1 151.0,155.6 135.6,165.2 135.2,175.5 132.8,180.5 137.6,156.2 136.8,177.9 136.1,175.7 140.3,148.0 135.8,181.7 142.8,150.1 141.2,181.2 142.6,149.3 147.8,200.0 145.8,183.0 149.8,180.1 150.1,175.3 149.6,175.1 147.4,172.2 145.5,172.9 147.2,173.6 147.3,171.9 163.3,169.7 152.1,172.9 144.7,179.3 146.7,181.7 149.0,175.2 146.5,179.2 155.4,181.8 152.3,176.4 148.5,180.4 150.3,175.8 150.4,175.6 152.3,174.9 152.8,174.1 152.0,178.6 149.1,177.5 145.9,179.5 144.0,179.8 150.1,177.8 151.2,178.5 151.9,175.0 154.9,178.8 149.1,186.8 144.2,186.6 153.9,183.7 152.6,185.1 151.6,185.4 156.0,178.7 152.4,179.9 150.0,175.4 151.8,178.9 152.0,180.7 152.4,175.9 152.9,176.5 153.0,177.7 153.1,183.1 152.5,176.7 151.9,176.9 153.9,175.5 154.2,176.0 150.5,180.3 151.5,180.4 148.7,176.5 147.6,180.0 149.8,184.3 151.9,184.1 151.2,185.4 154.9,179.9 155.2,180.0 156.9,176.7 154.8,175.4 149.6,175.5 140.8,176.4 135.3,173.8 135.7,173.2 135.9,172.1 135.6,167.0 134.2,175.3 133.3,170.0 133.9,179.7 133.7,158.6 135.5,190.3 132.0,165.5 131.9,164.7 136.1,194.1 149.0,178.7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></svg><span>Explore in 3D (about 2 MB)</span></button><div class=\"mvv\" data-mvv=\"scene\" data-mode=\"site\" data-src=\"/media/sensors/realsense-d456/views0.json\"></div></div></div>", "map": "<p>The solved positions and orientations, to scale in the IMU frame. Drag sideways to orbit. Tap a sensor to see its values.</p><div class=map><div class=stage><canvas id=rig tabindex=0 aria-label=\"3D map of the cameras and IMU\"></canvas><div class=tools><button data-view=iso type=button>3D</button><button data-view=front type=button>Front</button><button data-view=top type=button>Top</button><button data-view=side type=button>Side</button><button data-z=1 type=button aria-label=\"Zoom in\">+</button><button data-z=-1 type=button aria-label=\"Zoom out\">−</button></div></div><div class=panel><div class=picks id=picks></div><div id=info></div></div></div>", "hardware": "<div class=scroll><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Value</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Maker</td><td>RealSense (formerly Intel RealSense)</td><td><span class=chip>Maker</span></td></tr><tr><td>Camera module</td><td>RealSense Module D450 with the Vision Processor D4</td><td><span class=chip>Maker</span></td></tr><tr><td>Shutter</td><td>Global, on the infrared pair and the RGB camera</td><td><span class=chip>Maker</span></td></tr><tr><td>Infrared pair</td><td>87° × 58° depth field of view, 95 mm baseline; recorded here at 848×480, 30 Hz, both images on one stamp</td><td><span class=chip>Maker</span></td></tr><tr><td>RGB camera</td><td>1 MP, 90° × 65°, up to 1280×800 at 30 fps; recorded here at 848×480, 30 Hz</td><td><span class=chip>Maker</span></td></tr><tr><td>IMU</td><td>6-axis; gyro 400 Hz, accelerometer about 200 Hz in this recording</td><td><span class=chip>Measured</span></td></tr><tr><td>Enclosure</td><td>IP65: dust-tight and protected against water jets</td><td><span class=chip>Maker</span></td></tr><tr><td>Link</td><td>USB-C; 124 × 29 × 26 mm</td><td><span class=chip>Maker</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=note>Maker's specs from <a href=\"https://www.realsenseai.com/products/d456-usb/\">RealSense D456 page</a>, checked 2026-11-13.</p><p class=note>Company: <a href=\"https://www.realsenseai.com/\">RealSense</a>.</p>", "dataset": "<div class=two><div class=scroll><table><tbody><tr><td>Recording</td><td>1 recording, 90 s, hand-held. 2,700 frames per infrared camera, 2,699 RGB frames, 36,471 IMU samples</td></tr><tr><td>Format</td><td>ROS1 bag</td></tr><tr><td>Board</td><td>Chessboard shown on a screen, 10×7 squares (9×6 inner corners), 75 mm squares as measured by the recorder</td></tr><tr><td>Exposure</td><td>Fixed, about 2 ms on all three cameras; no auto exposure</td></tr><tr><td>Licence</td><td>CC BY-NC 4.0, for the data, clip and figures; commercial use by request</td></tr><tr><td>Hosted</td><td>Not hosted by us. Public on the Hugging Face Hub as nerako/mvis-d455-d456-chessboard, take D456_02</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div><figure class=board><svg viewBox=\"-75.0 -75.0 900.0 675.0\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Chessboard 7 by 10 squares, to scale\"><rect x=\"-75.0\" y=\"-75.0\" width=\"900.0\" height=\"675.0\" fill=\"#fff\"/><path fill=\"#111\" d=\"M0.00 0.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM150.00 0.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM300.00 0.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM450.00 0.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM600.00 0.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM75.00 75.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM225.00 75.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM375.00 75.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM525.00 75.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM675.00 75.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM0.00 150.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM150.00 150.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM300.00 150.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM450.00 150.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM600.00 150.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM75.00 225.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM225.00 225.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM375.00 225.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM525.00 225.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM675.00 225.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM0.00 300.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM150.00 300.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM300.00 300.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM450.00 300.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM600.00 300.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM75.00 375.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM225.00 375.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM375.00 375.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM525.00 375.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM675.00 375.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM0.00 450.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM150.00 450.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM300.00 450.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM450.00 450.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00zM600.00 450.00h75.00v75.00h-75.00z\"/></svg><figcaption>Chessboard 10 × 7 squares (9 × 6 inner corners), 75 mm squares, 750 × 525 mm. To scale</figcaption></figure></div></div>", "lens": "<div class=v data-v=\"0\"><p>Calibrated field of view, horizontal × vertical. cam0: 89° × 58°, corners reach 47° from the axis · cam1: 89° × 58°, corners reach 47° from the axis · cam2: 90° × 59°, corners reach 48° from the axis</p><div class=chart><svg viewBox=\"0 0 560 260\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Image radius against ray angle for each camera\"><line class=g x1=54.0 x2=54.0 y1=12 y2