284.5,104.9 301.0,91.7 317.5,76.4 333.9,57.9 350.4,34.2\"/></svg></div></div><p class=legend><i class=c0></i>cam0 <i class=c1></i>cam1 <i class=c2></i>cam2 </p><p class=note>We read these from the calibrated lens fit at the image edges, through the principal point (where the optical axis meets the image). ~ marks an axis past where the corners reached, so the fit is extrapolated there. Past the fit means an edge lies beyond where the fit holds, so we give no value.</p>", "imu": "<div class=v data-v=\"0\"><p>Each bar shows a scale as its deviation from 1. IMU model: calyx. <code>t_ga</code>, the time offset between the gyroscope and accelerometer channels: −4.89 ± 0.27 ms.</p><div class=bars><div class=bar><span>Gyro scale x</span><i><u style=\"left:50.00%;width:2.36%\"></u></i><b>+0.38 %</b></div><div class=bar><span>Gyro scale y</span><i><u style=\"left:50.00%;width:2.19%\"></u></i><b>+0.35 %</b></div><div class=bar><span>Gyro scale z</span><i><u style=\"left:48.72%;width:1.28%\"></u></i><b>−0.20 %</b></div><div class=bar><span>Accel scale x</span><i><u style=\"left:50.00%;width:5.49%\"></u></i><b>+0.88 %</b></div><div class=bar><span>Accel scale y</span><i><u style=\"left:50.00%;width:2.27%\"></u></i><b>+0.36 %</b></div><div class=bar><span>Accel scale z</span><i><u style=\"left:50.00%;width:5.51%\"></u></i><b>+0.88 %</b></div><div class=bar><span></span><em><s>−8 %</s><s>0</s><s>+8 %</s></em><b></b></div></div></div>", "timing": "<p>The time offsets, to scale. td is the camera–IMU time offset, with t_imu = t_cam + td.</p><div class=v data-v=\"0\"><div class=chart><svg viewBox=\"0 0 560 170\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Time offsets in milliseconds, to scale\"><line class=\"g\" x1=70.0 x2=70.0 y1=4 y2=146 /><text x=70.0 y=162 text-anchor=middle>-10 ms</text><line class=\"g\" x1=177.5 x2=177.5 y1=4 y2=146 /><text x=177.5 y=162 text-anchor=middle>-5 ms</text><line class=\"g z\" x1=285.0 x2=285.0 y1=4 y2=146 /><text x=285.0 y=162 text-anchor=middle>+0 ms</text><line class=\"g\" x1=392.5 x2=392.5 y1=4 y2=146 /><text x=392.5 y=162 text-anchor=middle>+5 ms</text><line class=\"g\" x1=500.0 x2=500.0 y1=4 y2=146 /><text x=500.0 y=162 text-anchor=middle>+10 ms</text><text x=0 y=22>cam0 td</text><line class=stem x1=285.0 x2=437.3 y1=18 y2=18 /><circle class=dot cx=437.3 cy=18 r=5 /><text x=446.3 y=22 text-anchor=start>+7.08</text><text x=0 y=56>cam1 td</text><line class=stem x1=285.0 x2=437.3 y1=52 y2=52 /><circle class=dot cx=437.3 cy=52 r=5 /><text x=446.3 y=56 text-anchor=start>+7.08</text><text x=0 y=90>cam2 td</text><line class=stem x1=285.0 x2=414.5 y1=86 y2=86 /><circle class=dot cx=414.5 cy=86 r=5 /><text x=423.5 y=90 text-anchor=start>+6.03</text><text x=0 y=124>t_ga</text><line class=stem x1=285.0 x2=179.8 y1=120 y2=120 /><circle class=dot cx=179.8 cy=120 r=5 /><text x=170.8 y=124 text-anchor=end>−4.89</text></svg></div></div>", "results": "<p>Rotation is log(R) in rad, camera in the IMU frame.</p><div class=v data-v=\"0\"><div class=scroll><table class=num><thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>MVIS</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=grp><th colspan=2>cam0</th></tr><tr><td>fx px</td><td>429.63</td></tr><tr><td>fy px</td><td>430.04</td></tr><tr><td>cx px</td><td>426.80</td></tr><tr><td>cy px</td><td>241.14</td></tr><tr><td>k1</td><td>−0.00188</td></tr><tr><td>k2</td><td>−0.00180</td></tr><tr><td>k3</td><td>0.00020</td></tr><tr><td>k4</td><td>0.00141</td></tr><tr><td>Lever x mm</td><td>−27.04</td></tr><tr><td>Lever y mm</td><td>+6.84</td></tr><tr><td>Lever z mm</td><td>+21.97</td></tr><tr><td>log(R) rad</td><td>[+0.0072, +0.0108, +0.0059]</td></tr><tr><td>td ms</td><td>+7.083</td></tr><tr><td>Reprojection px</td><td>0.105</td></tr><tr class=grp><th colspan=2>cam1</th></tr><tr><td>fx px</td><td>429.39</td></tr><tr><td>fy px</td><td>429.81</td></tr><tr><td>cx px</td><td>426.78</td></tr><tr><td>cy px</td><td>241.39</td></tr><tr><td>k1</td><td>−0.00098</td></tr><tr><td>k2</td><td>−0.00203</td></tr><tr><td>k3</td><td>0.00041</td></tr><tr><td>k4</td><td>0.00094</td></tr><tr><td>Lever x mm</td><td>+67.38</td></tr><tr><td>Lever y mm</td><td>+7.43</td></tr><tr><td>Lever z mm</td><td>+21.33</td></tr><tr><td>log(R) rad</td><td>[+0.0069, +0.0090, +0.0059]</td></tr><tr><td>td ms</td><td>+7.084</td></tr><tr><td>Reprojection px</td><td>0.085</td></tr><tr class=grp><th colspan=2>cam2</th></tr><tr><td>fx px</td><td>426.73</td></tr><tr><td>fy px</td><td>426.57</td></tr><tr><td>cx px</td><td>429.41</td></tr><tr><td>cy px</td><td>246.78</td></tr><tr><td>k1</td><td>−0.05057</td></tr><tr><td>k2</td><td>0.03740</td></tr><tr><td>k3</td><td>0.00024</td></tr><tr><td>k4</td><td>0.00203</td></tr><tr><td>Lever x mm</td><td>+31.58</td></tr><tr><td>Lever y mm</td><td>+6.97</td></tr><tr><td>Lever z mm</td><td>+21.66</td></tr><tr><td>log(R) rad</td><td>[+0.0092, +0.0078, +0.0050]</td></tr><tr><td>td ms</td><td>+6.025</td></tr><tr><td>Reprojection px</td><td>0.099</td></tr><tr class=grp><th colspan=2>IMU</th></tr><tr><td>t_ga ms</td><td>−4.89 ± 0.27</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>", "limits": "<ul class=list><li>One recording, with no independent reference on this page. These values show what MVIS solved, not how close they are to the truth.</li><li>The square size is the recorder&#x27;s own measurement of a board shown on a screen. It scales every baseline and lever arm; the solved stereo baseline comes out about 0.7 % under the 95 mm the maker lists, which a square of about 75.5 mm would explain. Not confirmed.</li><li>The infrared images are the camera&#x27;s own rectified output, so their distortion is close to zero by construction and the values describe that output, not the bare lens.</li><li>The recorder turned the camera&#x27;s IMU correction off, so the IMU scale and bias values are those of the raw sensor. The accelerometer was resampled onto the gyro&#x27;s time stamps before the solve.</li></ul>", "run": "<ul class=list><li>Left infrared, right infrared and RGB cameras with the IMU in one solve, all three treated as global shutter. Pinhole camera with radial-tangential distortion, seeded from three single-camera solves of the same recording and left free; camera time offsets, IMU scale and misalignment and the gyro-to-accel offset t_ga estimated. The board is kept rigid. IMU noise is the MVIS default, since no measured values exist for this unit. Solved 2026-11-13.</li></ul>", "header": "<div class=sd><div class=sd-grid><div class=sd-head><a class=sd-maker href=\"https://www.realsenseai.com/products/d456-usb/\">RealSense ↗︎</a><h1 id=\"_top\">RealSense D456</h1><p class=sd-type>Depth camera: global-shutter infrared stereo and RGB with a 6-axis IMU</p></div><figure class=sd-plate><div class=sd-frame><img src=\"/media/sensors/realsense-d456/realsense-d456.jpg\" alt=\"RealSense D456 depth camera with water splashing over it\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\"></div><figcaption><a href=\"https://www.realsenseai.com/products/d456-usb/\">Photo: RealSense, D456 product page ↗︎</a></figcaption></figure><div class=sd-cta><div class=sd-buttons><a class=\"sd-btn primary\" href=\"https://www.realsenseai.com/products/d456-usb/\">RealSense product page ↗︎</a><a class=sd-btn href=\"#specifications\">All specs (9) ↓</a></div><p class=sd-more><a href=\"https://github.com/realsenseai/librealsense\">SDK ↗︎</a></p></div><div class=sd-specs><dl class=sd-rows><div class=sd-row><dt>Cameras</dt><dd>848 × 480 here: IR stereo + RGB<span class=sd-tag>Measured</span></dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>Shutter</dt><dd>Global<a class=sd-tag href=\"https://www.realsenseai.com/products/d456-usb/\">Maker ↗︎</a></dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>Field of view</dt><dd>Calibrated 89° × 58°<span class=sd-tag>Measured</span><br>87° × 58° depth, 90° × 65° RGB<a class=sd-tag href=\"https://www.realsenseai.com/products/d456-usb/\">Maker ↗︎</a></dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>Baseline</dt><dd>94.4 mm<span class=sd-tag>Measured</span></dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>IMU</dt><dd>6-axis, gyro 400 Hz, accel 200 Hz<span class=sd-tag>Measured</span></dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>Output</dt><dd>USB-C, ROS bag<a class=sd-tag href=\"https://www.realsenseai.com/products/d456-usb/\">Maker ↗︎</a></dd></div></dl><p class=sd-foot>Maker values checked 2026-11-13 · 1 recording, 90 s · CC BY-NC 4.0</p></div></div></div>", "specifications": "<div class=scroll><table class=spec-table><tbody><tr class=grp><th colspan=2>Published by the maker</th></tr><tr><td>Maker</td><td>RealSense (formerly Intel RealSense)</td></tr><tr><td>Camera module</td><td>RealSense Module D450 with the Vision Processor D4</td></tr><tr><td>Shutter</td><td>Global, on the infrared pair and the RGB camera</td></tr><tr><td>Infrared pair</td><td>87° × 58° depth field of view, 95 mm baseline; recorded here at 848×480, 30 Hz, both images on one stamp</td></tr><tr><td>RGB camera</td><td>1 MP, 90° × 65°, up to 1280×800 at 30 fps; recorded here at 848×480, 30 Hz</td></tr><tr><td>Enclosure</td><td>IP65: dust-tight and protected against water jets</td></tr><tr><td>Link</td><td>USB-C; 124 × 29 × 26 mm</td></tr><tr class=grp><th colspan=2>Measured in these recordings</th></tr><tr><td>IMU</td><td>6-axis; gyro 400 Hz, accelerometer about 200 Hz in this recording</td></tr><tr><td>Calibrated field of view</td><td>cam0 89° × 58° · cam1 89° × 58° · cam2 90° × 59°</td></tr></tbody></table></div>", "rig": "<p>The solved rig in 3D, to scale. Tap a sensor to see its values. In full screen you can rotate and zoom. Grid squares are 20 mm.</p><div class=map><div class=stage><canvas id=rig tabindex=0 aria-label=\"3D map of the cameras and IMU\"></canvas><div class=tools><button data-view=iso type=button>3D</button><button data-view=front type=button>Front</button><button data-view=top type=button>Top</button><button data-view=side type=button>Side</button><button data-z=1 type=button aria-label=\"Zoom in\">+</button><button data-z=-1 type=button aria-label=\"Zoom out\">−</button></div></div><div class=panel><div class=picks id=picks></div><div id=info></di